125 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 92 0 R
/E (The Multithreaded Linux Application Using POSIX Threads and Mutexes is designed to demonstrate the concepts of concurrent programming in a Linux environment. The application uses POSIX Threads \(Pthreads\) to execute multiple tasks concurrently, improving responsiveness and resource utilization. Since multiple threads may access shared resources simultaneously, mutexes \(mutual exclusion locks\) are used to prevent race conditions and maintain data consistency. The project demonstrates thread creation, execution, synchronization, shared-resource management, and proper thread termination. It provides a practical understanding of how multithreading and synchronization mechanisms are implemented in Linux using the C programming language.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
